{"name":"Cannery Park","hex":"#bcb09e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cannery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A factory that produces canned goods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cannery"},{"term":"park","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of land set aside for environment preservation or recreation.","A tract of ground kept in its natural state, about or adjacent to a residence, such as for the preservation of game, for walking, riding, or the like."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bring (something such as a vehicle) to a halt or store in a specified place.","To defer (a matter) until a later date."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/park"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canning","blocks":[{"text":"Canning is a method of food preservation in which food is processed and sealed in an airtight container. Canning provides a shelf life that typically ranges from one to five years, although under specific circumstances, it can be much longer. A freeze-dried canned product, such as canned dried lentils, could last as long as 30 years in an edible state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/FMIB_34482_Making_Salmon_Cans.jpeg/330px-FMIB_34482_Making_Salmon_Cans.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canning","wikidata":"Q843389"},{"title":"Park","blocks":[{"text":"A park is an area of natural, semi-natural or planted space set aside for human enjoyment and recreation or for the protection of wildlife or natural habitats. Urban parks are green spaces set aside for recreation inside towns and cities. National parks and country parks are green spaces used for recreation in the countryside. State parks and provincial parks are administered by sub-national government states and agencies. Parks may consist of grassy areas, rocks, soil and trees, but may also contain buildings and other artifacts such as monuments, fountains or playground structures. Many parks have fields for playing sports such as baseball and football, and paved areas for games such as basketball. Many parks have trails for walking, biking and other activities. Some parks are built adjacent to bodies of water or watercourses and may comprise a beach or boat dock area. Urban parks often have benches for sitting and may contain picnic tables and barbecue grills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Halleyparknovember_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Halleyparknovember_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park","wikidata":"Q22698"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Boutappertcolljpb.jpg/500px-Boutappertcolljpb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Boutappertcolljpb.jpg/500px-Boutappertcolljpb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A canning jar used by Nicolas Appert's canning factory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoutappertcolljpb.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Berthold_Weiss_Canned_Foods.jpg/500px-Berthold_Weiss_Canned_Foods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Berthold_Weiss_Canned_Foods.jpg/500px-Berthold_Weiss_Canned_Foods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Berthold-Weiss Factory, one of the first large canned food factories in Csepel, Budapest (1885)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerthold_Weiss_Canned_Foods.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Cannery_worker_filling_tuna_cans%2C_Los_Angeles_Cannery_Co.%2C_Long_Beach%